Qore JNI packages for the testing PPA
====================================

Qore native code, bridge classes, providers and test fixtures build from source.
Third-party JARs are pinned upstream binaries. Their URLs, checksums, source
archives and licensing metadata are recorded in debian/java-dependencies.json.
Rebuilding those dependencies is not a release gate for this PPA. Debian archive
admission is a separate project and has stricter bundled-JAR requirements.

Prepare vendor/ before exporting the source package:

  python3 debian/prepare-vendor.py fetch

It downloads only pinned HTTPS inputs and verifies SHA-256. The build uses
verify and unpack-kotlin, which never access the network. Export vendor/ as
qore-jni-module_VERSION.orig-vendor.tar.xz alongside the main orig tarball.
The main tarball excludes the precompiled first-party test fixtures listed
in Files-Excluded; package tests rebuild them with the configured Java 21 JDK.

Every third-party provider JAR remains byte-for-byte unchanged from the tracked
input. Xerces has the documented upstream Qore removal of service registrations
needed to avoid Kotlin conflicts; all remaining members match Maven Central.
The Paho common JAR is the exact pinned snapshot published by Eclipse, despite
its shorter checked-in filename. No dependency is resolved from a floating URL.

The source component includes the corresponding source JARs and full LGPL
project source archives. Users can obtain it alongside this package from the
PPA source publication. Runtime packages include upstream license and copyright
notices. The private Kotlin installation is optional and does not replace a
system compiler. JARs remain replaceable files; no license restriction on
modification or reverse engineering is added by this package.

Native JNI links to the private OpenJDK 21 lib/server directory using RUNPATH.
The explicit openjdk-21-jre-headless dependency supplies that unversioned JVM
library. No global ldconfig setting or environment variable is required.
Qore compiler metadata, source and AOT providers, resources and translations
are included. AOT metadata survives stripping and debug symbols are separate.

Only Ubuntu 26.04 amd64 with the matching Qore testing SDK is initially being
qualified. Other targets, the final Qore ABI and security review remain release
requirements. Pinned Java/Kotlin dependencies need ongoing security updates.
